{
  "abstract": "Repeated uses of the diagonal parity phase from the roots of X⁴−X−1 on the balanced two-qubit product state give squared concurrences dense in the unit interval after every finite cutoff. No finite iterate has the two-step Hardy-optimal Schmidt spectrum. An explicit population change on the first qubit gives that spectrum in one use of the same gate.",
